From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: elkir0 <elkir0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: gts28ltexx: GPU devfreq in the daily board, capped at
 420 MHz

Include exynos5433-gts28ltexx-gpufreq.dtsi in the board, after
exynos5433-gts28ltexx-gpu.dtsi (which deletes the GPU's
operating-points-v2; the gpufreq dtsi sets it again), as the test
branch does, and cap the GPU at 420 MHz in the device tree.

Why 420 MHz: mainline never programs the G3D adaptive body bias, and
PMU + 0x0790 reads 0x8000008d on the tablet, stock's idle reverse-bias
value, where stock runs the GPU at 0x80000088.  Until the kernel writes
that value at G3D power-on, the of 2026-10-29 chose 420 MHz
for the daily kernel (Omarchy repo docs/ONDEVICE-2026-10-29.md, "GPU
frequency:").  The kernel is shared by the Phosh and the
Omarchy root images, so the cap is in the device tree, not in a udev
rule.

The board deletes the 500, 550, 600 and 700 MHz OPPs after the include
and overrides every GPU cooling-map, so the gpufreq dtsi stays the full
8-OPP design for test builds and for raising the cap later.  With 4
OPPs the devfreq cooling states are 0 = 420, 1 = 350, 2 = 266,
3 = 160 MHz (max_state 3; the dtsi's states 4-7 would fail to bind):

  trip              dtsi (8 OPPs)     board (4 OPPs)
  apollo  81 C      4 (420 MHz)       1 (350 MHz)
  apollo  86 C      7 (160 MHz)       3 (160 MHz)
  g3d     95 C      4 (420 MHz)       1 (350 MHz)
  g3d    100 C      5 (350 MHz)       2 (266 MHz)
  g3d    105 C      6 (266 MHz)       3 (160 MHz)
  g3d    110 C      7 (160 MHz)       3 (160 MHz)

The g3d trips stay inert while tmu_g3d is disabled.  Hot and critical
trips are unchanged.

Fold the two settings of gts28ltexx_gpufreq.config that the defconfig
lacked (DEVFREQ_GOV_SIMPLE_ONDEMAND=y, DEVFREQ_THERMAL=y) into
gts28ltexx_defconfig, plus PM_DEVFREQ=y for clarity (panfrost already
selects it), so the daily build needs no fragment.  The fragment stays,
now redundant.  Comments of the gpu and gpufreq dtsi updated.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../samsung/exynos5433-gts28ltexx-gpu.dtsi    | 23 +++---
 .../exynos5433-gts28ltexx-gpufreq.dtsi        | 19 +++--
 .../dts/samsung/exynos5433-gts28ltexx.dts     | 74 ++++++++++++++++++-
 arch/arm/configs/gts28ltexx_defconfig         | 11 +++
 arch/arm/configs/gts28ltexx_gpufreq.config    |  3 +
 5 files changed, 114 insertions(+), 16 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/samsung/exynos5433-gts28ltexx-gpu.dtsi b/arch/arm/boot/dts/samsung/exynos5433-gts28ltexx-gpu.dtsi
index 9bbbbebab..aac5bd86a 100644
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/samsung/exynos5433-gts28ltexx-gpu.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/samsung/exynos5433-gts28ltexx-gpu.dtsi
@@ -6,6 +6,9 @@
  * mainline panfrost driver, with no frequency or voltage scaling: the GPU
  * runs at the clock the G3D clock unit already has, on BUCK6 at the voltage
  * the bootloader left.  docs/GPU.md has the source table and the reasoning.
+ * The board then includes exynos5433-gts28ltexx-gpufreq.dtsi, which sets
+ * a new OPP table and turns scaling on (capped at 420 MHz by the board,
+ * docs/GPU.md section 10).
  *
  * Stock reference (01_dumps/live_fdt.dts:1830-1836, node "mali"): same
  * registers (0x14ac0000, 0x5000), same interrupts in the same order (SPI
@@ -21,21 +24,23 @@ &gpu {
 	 * and the regulator the stock Mali platform code drives
 	 * (kernel_universal5433 drivers/gpu/arm/t7xx/r22p0/platform/exynos/
 	 * gpu_exynos5433.c:683, regulator_get(NULL, "vdd_g3d")).  The board
-	 * file keeps it always-on at the bootloader voltage (600-1500 mV
-	 * window, no voltage request from anyone).  With no OPP table below,
+	 * file keeps it always-on (600-1500 mV window).  With no OPP table,
 	 * panfrost only takes an enable reference on it
-	 * (panfrost_device.c:86-117, 225-230) and never sets a voltage.
-	 * The phandle also orders the GPU probe after the PMIC.
+	 * (panfrost_device.c:86-117, 225-230), never sets a voltage, and the
+	 * rail stays at the bootloader voltage; with the gpufreq dtsi's
+	 * table, panfrost sets the OPP voltages.  The phandle also orders the
+	 * GPU probe after the PMIC.
 	 */
 	mali-supply = <&buck6_reg>;
 	status = "okay";
 
 	/*
-	 * No OPP table, hence no devfreq: panfrost_devfreq_init() returns 0
-	 * when the device has no table (panfrost_devfreq.c:151-157) and the
-	 * GPU keeps the clock rate it finds at probe.  The SoC table is the
-	 * stock Mali driver's default table (gpu_exynos5433.c:46-55); stock
-	 * replaces its voltages by per-chip ASV values at boot
+	 * The SoC's OPP table is deleted (the gpufreq dtsi sets another one).
+	 * Without a table there is no devfreq: panfrost_devfreq_init()
+	 * returns 0 when the device has no table (panfrost_devfreq.c:151-157)
+	 * and the GPU keeps the clock rate it finds at probe.  The SoC table
+	 * is the stock Mali driver's default table (gpu_exynos5433.c:46-55);
+	 * stock replaces its voltages by per-chip ASV values at boot
 	 * (gpu_dvfs_governor.c:263-284), and at 700 MHz it is below the
 	 * stock value of the slowest group in table version 1 (1150000 vs
 	 * 1162500 uV, mach/asv-exynos5433.h:539).  This chip's ASV group is
diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/samsung/exynos5433-gts28ltexx-gpufreq.dtsi b/arch/arm/boot/dts/samsung/exynos5433-gts28ltexx-gpufreq.dtsi
index d2c1a6cfb..29f1e03f7 100644
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/samsung/exynos5433-gts28ltexx-gpufreq.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/samsung/exynos5433-gts28ltexx-gpufreq.dtsi
@@ -3,11 +3,17 @@
  * Samsung Galaxy Tab S2 8.0 LTE (SM-T715), Exynos5433 - GPU frequency
  * scaling (panfrost devfreq) and GPU thermal throttling
  *
- * NOT included by the board yet.  Include it AFTER
- * exynos5433-gts28ltexx-gpu.dtsi (that file deletes the GPU's
- * operating-points-v2 property, this one sets it again), together with
- * arch/arm/configs/gts28ltexx_gpufreq.config.  docs/GPU.md section 10
- * has the value-by-value source table and the device test plan.
+ * The full design: 8 OPPs, 160-700 MHz, cooling states numbered for
+ * 8 OPPs.  The board includes it AFTER exynos5433-gts28ltexx-gpu.dtsi
+ * (that file deletes the GPU's operating-points-v2 property, this one
+ * sets it again).  The devfreq options it needs are in
+ * gts28ltexx_defconfig (arch/arm/configs/gts28ltexx_gpufreq.config, which
+ * has the same options, is now redundant).  The daily board caps the GPU
+ * at 420 MHz: after the include it deletes the 500, 550, 600 and 700 MHz
+ * OPPs and renumbers every GPU cooling-map (exynos5433-gts28ltexx.dts,
+ * section 12).  Keep this file whole so that test builds can use all 8
+ * OPPs.  docs/GPU.md section 10 has the value-by-value source table and
+ * the device test plan, section 10.11 the daily cap.
  *
  * Path abbreviations in the comments:
  *   stock/   = 02_sources/kernel_universal5433/
@@ -78,7 +84,8 @@
  * drivers/thermal/devfreq_cooling.c:348-375, 110): 0 = 700, 1 = 600,
  * 2 = 550, 3 = 500, 4 = 420, 5 = 350, 6 = 266, 7 = 160 MHz.  The
  * cooling-maps below use these numbers: renumber them if an OPP is added,
- * removed or disabled.
+ * removed or disabled (the daily board does, for its 420 MHz cap:
+ * 0 = 420, 1 = 350, 2 = 266, 3 = 160 MHz).
  */
 / {
 	gpu_opp_table_gts28: opp-table-gpu {
diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/samsung/exynos5433-gts28ltexx.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/samsung/exynos5433-gts28ltexx.dts
index 6f8ec3153..423e26b4a 100644
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/samsung/exynos5433-gts28ltexx.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/samsung/exynos5433-gts28ltexx.dts
@@ -847,12 +847,84 @@ &framebuffer {
 /* ==================================================================== */
 
 /*
- * No OPP table: Linux never changes the GPU voltage or clock (docs/GPU.md).
  * Validated on the tablet on 2026-10-28: Mali-T760 id 0x750 r0p1, 6 shader
  * cores, boot clock 266 MHz with vdd_g3d (BUCK6) at 937 500 uV, Mesa
  * "Mali-T760 MC6 (Panfrost)" GLES 3.1 renderer in phoc, no GPU faults.
+ *
+ * Frequency scaling: the OPP table, panfrost as a devfreq cooling device
+ * and the GPU passive trips come from exynos5433-gts28ltexx-gpufreq.dtsi
+ * (docs/GPU.md section 10); the devfreq options are in
+ * gts28ltexx_defconfig.  It must come after exynos5433-gts28ltexx-gpu.dtsi:
+ * that file deletes the GPU's operating-points-v2 property, the gpufreq
+ * one sets it again.
  */
 #include "exynos5433-gts28ltexx-gpu.dtsi"
+#include "exynos5433-gts28ltexx-gpufreq.dtsi"
+
+/*
+ * Daily cap: 420 MHz (docs/GPU.md section 10.11).  Mainline never
+ * programs the G3D adaptive body bias: PMU + 0x0790 keeps 0x8000008d,
+ * the reverse bias stock applies only while the GPU idles, where stock
+ * runs the GPU at 0x80000088 (no bias).  Until the kernel writes that
+ * value at G3D power-on, the four fastest OPPs of the gpufreq dtsi are
+ * deleted.  They are deleted here and not in the dtsi, so that file
+ * stays the full design (8 OPPs, 160-700 MHz) for test builds and for
+ * raising the cap later.  The cap is in the device tree, not in a udev
+ * rule, because this kernel is shared by the Phosh and Omarchy root
+ * images.
+ */
+&gpu_opp_table_gts28 {
+	/delete-node/ opp-500000000;
+	/delete-node/ opp-550000000;
+	/delete-node/ opp-600000000;
+	/delete-node/ opp-700000000;
+};
+
+/*
+ * GPU cooling states, renumbered for the 4 remaining OPPs.  devfreq
+ * cooling counts from the fastest OPP (drivers/thermal/devfreq_cooling.c):
+ * 0 = 420, 1 = 350, 2 = 266, 3 = 160 MHz, max_state 3.  The gpufreq dtsi
+ * numbers its maps for 8 OPPs (states 4-7): a state above 3 would make
+ * the binding fail (thermal_of.c), so every GPU map is overridden here.
+ * A state-0 cap would do nothing at 420 MHz, so each trip caps one step
+ * below the dtsi's level, down to 160 MHz:
+ *   apollo  81 C: 420 -> 350 MHz (1)    86 C: 160 MHz (3)
+ *   g3d     95 C: 420 -> 350 MHz (1)   100 C: 350 -> 266 MHz (2)
+ *          105 C: 266 -> 160 MHz (3)   110 C: 160 MHz (3)
+ * The g3d trips stay inert while tmu_g3d is disabled.  The hot and
+ * critical trips (exynos5433-gts28ltexx-thermal.dtsi) are unchanged.
+ */
+&g3d_thermal {
+	cooling-maps {
+		map-gpu-throttle1 {
+			cooling-device = <&gpu 1 1>;
+		};
+
+		map-gpu-throttle2 {
+			cooling-device = <&gpu 2 2>;
+		};
+
+		map-gpu-throttle3 {
+			cooling-device = <&gpu 3 3>;
+		};
+
+		map-gpu-throttle4 {
+			cooling-device = <&gpu 3 3>;
+		};
+	};
+};
+
+&apollo_thermal {
+	cooling-maps {
+		map-gpu-throttle1 {
+			cooling-device = <&gpu 1 1>;
+		};
+
+		map-gpu-throttle4 {
+			cooling-device = <&gpu 3 3>;
+		};
+	};
+};
 
 /* ==================================================================== */
 /* 13. Bluetooth (BCM4358 on UART3, hci_bcm)                            */
diff --git a/arch/arm/configs/gts28ltexx_defconfig b/arch/arm/configs/gts28ltexx_defconfig
index d42856ce2..8f716529d 100644
--- a/arch/arm/configs/gts28ltexx_defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm/configs/gts28ltexx_defconfig
@@ -173,6 +173,17 @@ CONFIG_RMI4_F12=y
 # RECOVERY again).  Loaded by hand / by the initramfs after the guard.
 CONFIG_DRM_PANFROST=m
 
+# GPU frequency scaling (docs/GPU.md section 10; the board includes
+# exynos5433-gts28ltexx-gpufreq.dtsi, capped at 420 MHz), folded in from
+# gts28ltexx_gpufreq.config.  PM_DEVFREQ is also selected by panfrost and
+# selects PM_OPP.  panfrost's governor built in, so devfreq_add_device()
+# needs no request_module() at panfrost load (drivers/devfreq/devfreq.c);
+# the devfreq cooling device, without which the GPU cooling-maps never
+# bind (include/linux/devfreq_cooling.h stub).
+CONFIG_PM_DEVFREQ=y
+CONFIG_DEVFREQ_GOV_SIMPLE_ONDEMAND=y
+CONFIG_DEVFREQ_THERMAL=y
+
 # Requested by the Omarchy (Hyprland) track, built in because the rootfs
 # ships no modules.  Firewall for ufw / iptables-nft (omarchy-mobile's
 # kernel fragment):
diff --git a/arch/arm/configs/gts28ltexx_gpufreq.config b/arch/arm/configs/gts28ltexx_gpufreq.config
index b8071feb8..e32bbcfe6 100644
--- a/arch/arm/configs/gts28ltexx_gpufreq.config
+++ b/arch/arm/configs/gts28ltexx_gpufreq.config
@@ -5,6 +5,9 @@
 # scripts/kbuild-mainline.sh --fragment), together with
 # arch/arm/boot/dts/samsung/exynos5433-gts28ltexx-gpufreq.dtsi.
 # docs/GPU.md section 10 has the rationale and the device test plan.
+# These options are now also in gts28ltexx_defconfig (the board includes
+# the dtsi), so merging this fragment changes nothing; kept for builds of
+# older trees.
 
 # panfrost stays a module, as in gts28ltexx_defconfig: built in, its probe
 # runs before the initramfs watchdog guard, and the first built-in boot
